    "rationale": "Most symbols are best treated as opaque lexical items: the two-letter fault/state codes do not show recurring substrings with stable, compositional meanings, and several standalone symbols explicitly mean whole stored procedures or context-dependent instructions ('same action as before'), which fails the productive paradigm test. Two small paradigms are defensible. First, K-trace/B-trace/S-trace form a clear shared frame __-trace with contrasting instrument fillers whose meanings match the whole-code contrasts; standalone trace remains lexical because no nonempty two-morpheme segmentation is supported for it. Second, x2/x3 support x + COUNT because the numeral contributes literal repetition count in the same frame. Candidate 'rs' and 'al' families are rejected: their residues do not form a coherent substitution class with predictable meanings.",
